---
import RichText from "@/components/RichText.astro";
import HomePageLayout from "@/layouts/HomePageLayout.astro";
---

<HomePageLayout
  description="Hi! I'm Joost Kersjes, currently working at Awareways as the Frontend Lead."
>
  <RichText>
    <h1>Joost Kersjes</h1>
    <p>
      Hi! I&apos;m Joost Kersjes, currently working at <a
        href="https://awareways.com/en/"
        target="_blank">Awareways</a
      > as the Frontend Lead.
    </p>
    <p>
      Professionally, I aim to build spotless user experiences. Here are some of
      the tools, languages and frameworks I love working with:<ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.typescriptlang.org/" target="_blank"
            >TypeScript</a
          >
        </li>
        <li><a href="https://vuejs.org/" target="_blank">Vue.js</a></li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://tanstack.com/query/latest" target="_blank"
            >TanStack Query</a
          >
        </li>
        <li><a href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank">Astro</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://prettier.io/" target="_blank">Prettier</a></li>
      </ul>
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="interests">
      <h2 id="interests">
        <a href="#interests">My interests</a>
      </h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          PC gaming, lots of games, to name a few:<ul>
            <li>
              Most often <a
                href="https://worldofwarcraft.blizzard.com/en-us/"
                target="_blank">World of Warcarft</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              My all-time favourite game is <a
                href="https://www.artofrally.com/"
                target="_blank">art of rally</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              Competitive games with friends e.g. <a
                href="https://www.marvelrivals.com/">Marvel Rivals</a
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>I watch every Formula 1 race (go Verstappen! go Williams!)</li>
        <li>
          Watching my friends stream games (<a
            href="https://www.twitch.tv/obsessedcommunity"
            target="_blank">their Twitch channel</a
          >)
        </li>
        <li>
          Making pizza from scratch (<a href="/pizza/">try my recipe</a>)
        </li>
        <li>League of Legends Esports (go G2!)</li>
        <li>
          Building LEGO Technic cars:<ul>
            <li>
              <a
                href="https://www.lego.com/en-nl/product/mclaren-formula-1-race-car-42141#pdp-features-accordion-title"
                >McLaren Formula 1&trade;</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <a
                href="https://www.lego.com/en-nl/product/lamborghini-sian-fkp-37-42115#pdp-features-accordion-title"
                >Lamborghini Sián</a
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="career">
      <h2 id="career">
        <a href="#career">My career so far</a>
      </h2>

      <h3>Awareways / 2021 - present</h3>
      <p>
        I joined Awareways at the very start of development for the <a
          href="https://awareways.com/en/wave/"
          target="_blank">Wave</a
        >
        learning platform which we ended up launching in 2022. As a fun side-project,
        I also got to host the <a
          href="https://connect.awareways.com/en/awarecast"
          target="_blank">Awarecast</a
        > podcast.
      </p>
      <p>
        While being mentored by <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/miguel-angelo-bento/"
          target="_blank">Miguel Bento</a
        >, which I'm very thankful for, I got to develop my skills in Vue.js,
        TypeScript, Cypress, Storybook, WCAG, Sass and Docker. It grew me in to
        a knowledgeble and well-rounded expert.
      </p>
      <p>
        After Awareways parted ways with Miguel in 2024, I took up the role of
        Frontend Lead, eventually hiring <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/claudiapereiraoliveira/"
          target="_blank">Cláudia Oliveira</a
        > to help contribute to our frontend projects. While building our new <a
          href="https://awareways.com/en/"
          target="_blank">Awareways website</a
        > in 2025 I grew fond of working with Astro.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm still working to improve my soft skills as a leader and a coach, but
        it is very motivating to have more responsibilities and I'm very excited
        for what the future holds for me at Awareways!
      </p>

      <h3>
        Spotler (<abbr title="formerly known as">f.k.a.</abbr> Webpower) / 2019 -
        2021
      </h3>
      <p>
        During my software development college education I had two internships
        with Webpower. I started working there part-time in 2019 and then
        full-time after I graduated in 2020.
      </p>
      <p>
        At Webpower I discovered my passion for frontend development and learned
        what it takes to build high-quality user experiences. My work mainly
        involved writing custom PHP scripts to process data, but working on the
        'flow builder' frontend application with React (JS) was what I enjoyed
        the most.
      </p>
      <p>
        After Webpower was aquired by Spotler Group in 2021, our team went
        through restructuring which made me think about my professional future.
        I started looking for a company that aligned with my values and would
        give me an opportunity to develop my frontend development expertise
        further. I found that at Awareways.
      </p>
    </section>
  </RichText>
</HomePageLayout>
